@lang en
-- The nine worked cases the brief names, asked through the record interface (`A period of time`, `Facts about an enactment`).
-- The expected answers are NOTES.md section 2, written from the text before any code ran.
-- Six period cases: the first has an answer on the text; five refuse, because the Act has no rule for a year, month or week that does not begin where the Schedule's definition begins it.
-- Three commencement cases: each has an answer on the text, and the first has a day but no moment.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      u IS A `Unit of time`
      h IS A `How a period is counted`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `A period of time`
`the test period` n u h d MEANS
    `A period of time` WITH
        `its length`                 IS n
        `its unit`                   IS u
        `how it is counted`          IS h
        `the day it is counted from` IS d

§ `Period case 1: thirty days from 2026-01-01`

#ASSERT `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30
#ASSERT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 30) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT `the day` (YMD 2026 1 31) `falls within the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))

§ `Period case 2: three years from 2025-07-16 (no rule for a year that does not begin on 1 January)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 3 Years `from a day` (YMD 2025 7 16)) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January"

§ `Period case 3: five years from 2025-01-15`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 5 Years `from a day` (YMD 2025 1 15)) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January"

§ `Period case 4: five years from 2025-09-01 (the first of a month, but not of a year)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 5 Years `from a day` (YMD 2025 9 1)) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January"

§ `Period case 5: two years from 2024-02-28`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 2 Years `from a day` (YMD 2024 2 28)) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January"

§ `Period case 6: one year from 2024-02-29 (the Act has no rule for 29 February)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 Years `from a day` (YMD 2024 2 29)) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of years that does not begin on 1 January"

§ `Period case 7: one month from 2025-01-31 (a month lacking the start day's number)`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `from a day` (YMD 2025 1 31)) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of calendar months that does not begin on the first day of a month"

§ `The same periods counted "after" an event: section 18(h) says nothing, so all refuse`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `after an event` (YMD 2026 1 1)) BECAUSE "section 18(h) says nothing about a period counted after an event"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 3 Years `after an event` (YMD 2025 7 16))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 5 Years `after an event` (YMD 2025 1 15))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 5 Years `after an event` (YMD 2025 9 1))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 2 Years `after an event` (YMD 2024 2 28))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 Years `after an event` (YMD 2024 2 29))
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 1 `Calendar months` `after an event` (YMD 2025 1 31))

§ `When the last day falls on a day of rest, recess or holiday: no rule, so the module refuses (the rest days are an input)`

-- 2026-01-30 is a Friday; 2026-01-31 a Saturday. Thirty days from 2026-01-02 ends on Saturday 2026-01-31.
#ASSERT `the last day of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 2)) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (`the last day of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 2))) (GIVEN x YIELD NOT `is weekday` x) BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a last day that falls on a day of rest, recess or holiday; another enactment or rules of court may have one"
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (`the last day of the period` (`the test period` 30 Days `from a day` (YMD 2026 1 1))) (GIVEN x YIELD NOT `is weekday` x) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 30

§ `Commencement case 1: an Act passed (the Bill signed) on 2026-03-10 that says nothing`

`the Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`
        `what it says about commencement`  IS `it says nothing about when it comes into operation`
        `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

#ASSERT `the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `the Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `the Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` BECAUSE "section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing"

§ `Commencement case 2: an Act expressed to come into operation on a day fixed later as 2026-06-01`

`the Act fixed for 1 June 2026` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`
        `what it says about commencement`  IS `it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 6 1)
        `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `the Act fixed for 1 June 2026`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` `the Act fixed for 1 June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1

§ `Commencement case 3: a statutory instrument made on 2026-03-10 that says nothing`

`the instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026` MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS `a statutory instrument`
        `what it says about commencement`  IS `it says nothing about when it comes into operation`
        `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)

#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `the instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
#ASSERT `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` `the instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the first day on which a statutory instrument is in operation throughout` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
